# Trivy misconfiguration findings accepted for this project.
# Each entry includes an explanation of why the finding is acceptable here.

# DS002: Image should not be run as root.
# This Dockerfile intentionally starts as root so that entrypoint.sh can
# self-heal /data directory ownership at container startup — the same pattern
# used by PostgreSQL, Redis, Nginx, and many other production container images.
# Privileges are immediately dropped to UID 99 (nobody/users) via `setpriv`
# before exec-ing start.sh. Runtime hardening is applied at the Docker level
# via template.xml: --cap-drop=ALL, --security-opt no-new-privileges:true, etc.
DS002

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# gradio 4.44.1: accepted known vulnerabilities (reviewed 2026-10-29)
#
# Forge Neo's UI is written for gradio 4.x. Most of these are fixed only in
# gradio 5.x or 6.x, which Neo does not support; some have no fix at all.
# This image already upgrades Neo's gradio 4.40.0 to 4.44.1 (the last 4.x
# release), which fixes 5 more. The rest cannot be fixed here without breaking
# the WebUI.
#
# They are ignored only so the build gate can pass. They are NOT hidden: every
# one is listed with its impact in README.md, section "Known security issues".
# Mitigations: LAN-only use, login always on, HTTPS on by default.
#
# Each entry expires 2027-01-31, after which the build fails again until
# someone re-checks for a Forge Neo release that moves past gradio 4.x.
# Source: https://osv.dev (package gradio, version 4.44.1).
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
